// Robust COGO Test Script
// This script is designed to run cleanly without producing state or argument errors.

// 1. Clear the environment and any previous logs
CLEAR
LOG ON

// 2. Establish Control Points Let's create a few base points to work from.
NE 1 5000.0000 5000.0000 "Start Point"
NE 2 6000.0000 5000.0000 "North Reference"
NEZ 3 5000.0000 6000.0000 100.00 "East Reference"

// 3. Setup Station and Backsight
// Required before using BD, AD, or other station-relative commands
STN 1
BS 2

// 4. Create Points from Station
// BD <Pt> <Quad> <Brg> <Dist> [Desc] (Northeast quadrant 1, 45 degrees, 100 units)
BD 10 1 45.0000 100.00 "BD Point NE"
// AD <Point> <Angle> <Dist> [Desc] (Turn right 90 degrees from backsight, 150 units)
AD 11 90.0000 150.00 "AD Point East"

// 5. Intersections
// RKRK <PtNew> <P1> <Dist1> <P2> <Dist2>
RKRK 20 1 500.0 2 500.0

// AZAZ <PtNew> <Pt1> <Az1> <Pt2> <Az2> [Desc]
AZAZ 21 1 45.0000 2 135.0000 "Azimuth Intersection"

// LNLN <PtNew> <P1> <P2> <Off1> <P3> <P4> <Off2> [Desc]
LNLN 22 1 3 0.0 2 10 0.0 "Line Intersection"

// 6. Information & Calculations
INV 1 10
DIST 1 2
AZ 1 3
ANG 2 1 3

// 7. Figure Management
// Build a simple triangle and check its closure
BEG TRIANGLE
CONT 1
CONT 2
CONT 3
CONT 1
END
MAPCHECK TRIANGLE

// 8. Transformations
// Translate point 10 using the vector from 1 to 3
TRN 1 3 10

// 9. Cleanup & Save
// DEL 22
// Info "Point 22 deleted."
SAVE robust_session.cogo
LOG OFF
